LightGBM and Random Forest have the highest accuracy
difference between the clean symptoms accuracy and
corrupted symptoms accuracy. This means that they
don't perform well on data that is different from the
one that they were trained on.

The averages are : Logistic Regression, Multinomial
Naive Bayes and Gaussian Naive Bayes.

The machines who did not regress as soon as the data
got tricky and new are Bernoulli Naive Bayes (surprisingly)
and K-Nearest Neighbor.

